From: ChaosControl maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] ftrace: avoid unused built-in symbol names during record validation

The boot-time weak-function validation worker visits every fentry record.
It only uses lookup success and the symbol offset, but kallsyms_lookup also
scans the compressed name stream and expands an unused name for each record.
Full KCOV instrumentation magnifies that avoidable boot work.

For built-in addresses, use the existing offset-only lookup. Both paths
use get_symbol_pos and the same built-in-address predicate. Preserve the
original name lookup for all other addresses, including module/ftrace
fallbacks. Keep weak-record rejection and every tracing/coverage feature.
No watchdog or operational bound changes are involved.

--- a/kernel/trace/ftrace.c
+++ b/kernel/trace/ftrace.c
@@ -4325,14 +4325,20 @@
  */
 static int test_for_valid_rec(struct dyn_ftrace *rec)
 {
-	char str[KSYM_SYMBOL_LEN];
 	unsigned long offset;
-	const char *ret;
-
-	ret = kallsyms_lookup(rec->ip, NULL, &offset, NULL, str);
+	bool valid;
+
+	/* Built-in records need an offset, not a decompressed symbol name. */
+	if (is_ksym_addr(rec->ip)) {
+		valid = kallsyms_lookup_size_offset(rec->ip, NULL, &offset);
+	} else {
+		char str[KSYM_SYMBOL_LEN];
+
+		valid = kallsyms_lookup(rec->ip, NULL, &offset, NULL, str) != NULL;
+	}
 
 	/* Weak functions can cause invalid addresses */
-	if (!ret || offset > FTRACE_MCOUNT_MAX_OFFSET) {
+	if (!valid || offset > FTRACE_MCOUNT_MAX_OFFSET) {
 		rec->flags |= FTRACE_FL_DISABLED;
 		return 0;
 	}
